## 3. Module Breakdown

Each module is a responsibility within the storefront. The concrete technology
per module is in the TSD.

| Module | Responsibility | Reads from | Writes to |
|---|---|---|---|
| Storefront shell | Home, navigation, branding, layout, footer. | — | — |
| Catalog | Catalog listing + product detail (images, variants, price, materials). | Catalog source | — |
| Blog | Blog list + article rendering, SEO metadata. | Catalog source (articles) | — |
| Cart | Add/remove lines, choose variant, attach personalization + note, total. | (transient, buyer-driven) | (transient cart state) |
| Order submission | Collect buyer info + consent; format the order; deliver to the sink. | Cart | Notification sink |
| Notification | One-way delivery of the formatted order to the channel. | Order submission | Notification sink |
| Privacy | Consent capture + public privacy notice. | — | — |

There is intentionally **no** module for: checkout, payments, customer accounts,
order state machine, admin CRM, or inbound command parsing.

