## 4. Conceptual Data Model

There is **no database we own.** These are the conceptual entities the system
works with, sourced from Shopify or assembled transiently by the buyer.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    PRODUCT ||--o{ VARIANT : has
    PRODUCT ||--o{ IMAGE : has
    ARTICLE ||--|| COVER : has
    CART ||--o{ CARTLINE : contains
    CARTLINE }o--|| VARIANT : selects
    CARTLINE ||--o{ ATTRIBUTE : carries
    CART ||--|| NOTE : has

    PRODUCT {
        string name
        string description
        string materials
        money price_cop
        bool available
    }
    VARIANT {
        string option_name
        string option_value
    }
    ARTICLE {
        string title
        string content
        string author
        date publishedAt
        string category
    }
    CARTLINE {
        int quantity
    }
    ATTRIBUTE {
        string key
        string value
    }
    NOTE {
        string text
    }
```

Entity notes:

- **Product** — a piece in the catalog. Has many **Variants** (structured
  options: material, size) and many **Images**.
- **Article** — a blog post with a **Cover** and SEO fields.
- **Cart** — transient, buyer-assembled. Contains many **CartLines** and one
  cart-level **Note**.
- **CartLine** — selects one **Variant**, with a quantity and zero or more
  **Attributes** (free-text personalization: engraving, instructions).
- **OrderMessage** (not shown) — the formatted payload derived from the Cart plus
  buyer info (name, contact) and a timestamp. This is what the notification
  module delivers. It is **not persisted** — it exists only as the message body.

The exact field shapes and types are pinned in the TSD (which maps them to the
concrete API types and the message format).

