## 5. Data Flow

The primary flow — a buyer submitting an order:

```
1. Buyer browses → Storefront reads Product/Article from the catalog source.
2. Buyer opens a Product → sees Variants and the personalization field.
3. Buyer selects a Variant, types personalization → "Add to cart".
   (CartLine carries the Variant + quantity + Attributes.)
4. Buyer repeats for more items; sets a cart-level Note if desired.
5. Buyer opens the order form → enters name + contact + ticks consent.
6. Buyer clicks "Send order".
   a. Order submission reads the full Cart + buyer info + consent.
   b. The order formatter builds the OrderMessage
      (items, variants, personalization, note, buyer, total, timestamp).
   c. The notification module delivers the message to the channel.
   d. Idempotency: a duplicate click within the window is ignored.
7. Buyer sees the confirmation screen.
8. Shirley reads the message in the channel → closes on WhatsApp (off-system).
```

**Read paths** (catalog, blog) are cacheable and public. **Write path** (order
submission) is the only mutation; it is one-way into the channel and nothing
flows back to the storefront from it.

