## ChangeLog

### v2.1 → v3.0 (this refactor)
- **Document re-scoped to tool-agnostic design** per the SDD standard. All
  technology names (Next.js, Payload, Drizzle, framework choices, API routes,
  exact schemas) moved to the TSD.
- **Architecture simplified** to three components: storefront (presentation),
  catalog source (Shopify), notification sink (Telegram channel). Removed:
  Payload CRM, Telegram webhook, daily digest cron, payment webhook, Supabase.
- **Module breakdown rewritten** — new modules: storefront shell, catalog, blog,
  cart, order submission, notification, privacy. Removed: command handler,
  dispatch queue, photo-to-draft, daily digest.
- **Data model made conceptual** — entities only (Product, Variant, Article,
  Cart, CartLine, Attribute, Note, OrderMessage); no owned database, no schema.
  Exact shapes now live in the TSD.
- **Data flow rewritten** as the buyer-driven order submission flow.
- **Security rewritten** — removed webhook secret/token validation and command
  idempotency; added minimal-surface, server-side secrets, submission
  idempotency, PII minimization + consent, no-LLM surface.
- **Cross-reference matrix** updated to v3.0 BRD/PRD.
